plan_text='For a spring investigation, secure the spring vertically and record its unloaded length against a nearby ruler. Add a calibrated force and measure the new length after the spring settles. Subtract the unloaded length to obtain extension, then repeat at several safe forces. Use the same spring, the same reference points and the same reading method. Keep falling loads away from feet and avoid overloading the spring. Record force in newtons, unloaded and loaded length in millimetres, and calculated extension in millimetres. Plot extension vertically against force horizontally. Describe the trend from the plotted data; if a fitted straight line is suitable, its gradient has units of millimetres per newton. Do not call that gradient a spring constant: the spring constant uses force per extension.'
